y of red blood cells or hemoglobin in the blood. This condition can occur in cancer patients and may present various symptoms that require monitoring and treatment. In the context of patient care, anemia is a condition that patients may experience and is often addressed during their follow-up treatment.", "CA 19.9:CA 19.9 is a tumor marker that plays a crucial role in the diagnosis and monitoring of treatment for pancreatic cancer. It has a sensitivity and specificity of up to 92%, making it a valuable tool in the clinical assessment of this type of cancer.", "NM ABDOMINAL:NM abdominal is a medical procedure reserved for difficult cases, cystic neoplasms, and evaluation of bile ducts.", "PANCREATECTOMY DUODENAL:Pancreatectomy duodenal is a surgical procedure of choice for tumors located in the head of the pancreas.", "PANCREATECTOMY DISTAL:Pancreatectomy distal is a surgical procedure performed for tumors located in the body and tail of the pancreas.", "ADENOCARCINOMA OF PANCREAS:Adenocarcinoma of the pancreas is a type of cancer diagnosed in the patient, confirmed by a TAC abdominal scan.", "TAC ABDOMINAL:TAC abdominal is a diagnostic imaging procedure that confirmed the patient's diagnosis of pancreatic adenocarcinoma.", "RETINOPATHY DIABETIC:Diabetic retinopathy is a complication of diabetes that affects the eyes, diagnosed in the patient.", "POLYNEUROPATHY DIABETIC:Diabetic polyneuropathy is a complication of diabetes that affects the peripheral nerves, diagnosed in the patient.", "MICROINFARTO CEREBRAL:Microinfarto cerebral refers to a small stroke that the patient experienced in 2010 without lasting effects.", "GASTROSCOPIA:Gastroscopy is a medical procedure performed if there is suspicion that a tumor infiltrates the duodenum.", "COMA HIPOGLUCÉMICO:Coma hipoglucémico refers to a severe state of unconsciousness due to extremely low blood sugar levels experienced by the patient.", "HIPOGLUCEMIAS GRAVES:Graves hypoglycemia refers to severe episodes of low blood 